WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:08.124
As new employees,
I'd like your opinion on our commercial.

2
00:00:08.207 --> 00:00:10.751
I've paid to have it aired
during the Super Bowl.

3
00:00:10.835 --> 00:00:13.796
- Wow.
- Not on the same channel, of course.

4
00:00:16.215 --> 00:00:19.260
Interplanetary deliveries...
What a headache.

5
00:00:19.593 --> 00:00:21.762
Evans, where is that package from earth?

6
00:00:21.887 --> 00:00:22.888
Uh...

7
00:00:25.307 --> 00:00:27.101
I'm not Evans!

8
00:00:27.184 --> 00:00:29.603
He should have used Planet Express.

9
00:00:31.188 --> 00:00:34.358
When those other companies
aren't brave or foolhardy enough to go,

10
00:00:34.442 --> 00:00:37.486
trust Planet Express
for reliable, on-time delivery.

11
00:00:40.906 --> 00:00:43.993
Here's your package,
Mr. Horrible Gelatinous Blob.

12
00:00:44.118 --> 00:00:47.705
Good work, Evans.
You've got a future around here.

13
00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:52.626
Thank you, sir.

14
00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:55.254
Planet Express.
Our crew is replaceable,

15
00:00:55.337 --> 00:00:56.881
your package isn't.

16
00:00:58.883 --> 00:01:00.676
Are there really giant birds like that?

17
00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.888
No, no, that was all
just special effects.

18
00:01:03.971 --> 00:01:05.765
Now, let's have breakfast.

19
00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:08.059
I hope everyone likes eggs.

20
00:01:52.853 --> 00:01:55.272
I'm never going to get used
to the 31st century.

21
00:01:55.439 --> 00:01:56.774
Caffeinated bacon?

22
00:01:56.857 --> 00:01:58.734
Baconated grapefruit?

23
00:01:59.110 --> 00:02:00.444
Admiral Crunch?

24
00:02:00.569 --> 00:02:03.614
Well, if you don't like that
try some Archduke Chocula.

25
00:02:04.615 --> 00:02:06.075
Ah, Hermes.

26
00:02:06.158 --> 00:02:08.452
Crew, meet Hermes Conrad.

27
00:02:08.536 --> 00:02:10.746
He manages my delivery business.

28
00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:14.291
Pays the bills,
notifies next of kin, what have you.

29
00:02:14.417 --> 00:02:17.086
Someone come and drop this package
through the slot last night.

30
00:02:17.169 --> 00:02:18.796
Now, which one of you
is the captain?

31
00:02:18.879 --> 00:02:21.924
Oh, my. I haven't picked
a new captain yet.

32
00:02:22.007 --> 00:02:24.468
It's always so hard to choose.

33
00:02:24.802 --> 00:02:26.554
Ooh. Ooh, ooh, ooh!

34
00:02:29.557 --> 00:02:31.392
Mmm... You.

35
00:02:33.561 --> 00:02:37.398
Okay, Captain,
this is just a standard legal release

36
00:02:37.481 --> 00:02:40.735
protecting Planet Express from lawsuits
in the event of the unforeseen.

37
00:02:40.943 --> 00:02:42.778
- "Death by airlock failure."
- Mm-hmm.

38
00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.864
- "Death by brain parasite."
- Ya.

39
00:02:44.947 --> 00:02:46.490
"Death by sonic diarrhea."

40
00:02:46.574 --> 00:02:47.700
Oh, you don't want that.

41
00:02:47.992 --> 00:02:50.202
Look, I don't know
about your previous captains,

42
00:02:50.286 --> 00:02:52.663
but I intend to do
as little dying as possible.

43
00:02:54.915 --> 00:02:55.1000
Sign the paper.

44
00:02:56.375 --> 00:02:58.878
And now, Fry,
before you go into space

45
00:02:58.961 --> 00:03:01.255
you'll need to see our staff doctor.

46
00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:05.342
I should warn you, though,
he's a little unusual.

47
00:03:05.593 --> 00:03:07.053
He wears sandals.

48
00:03:11.182 --> 00:03:14.810
Dr. Zoidberg, this is Fry,
the new delivery boy.

49
00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:16.103
He needs a physical.

50
00:03:16.187 --> 00:03:17.855
Excellent, excellent.

51
00:03:20.357 --> 00:03:22.151
You'll be fine.

52
00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:27.823
Now, open your mouth
and let's have a look at that brain.

53
00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:30.117
No, no, no, not that mouth.

54
00:03:30.201 --> 00:03:31.494
I only have one.

55
00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:32.912
Really?

56
00:03:33.537 --> 00:03:36.040
Uh... Is there a human doctor around?

57
00:03:36.165 --> 00:03:38.626
Young lady, I'm an expert on humans.

58
00:03:38.709 --> 00:03:41.087
Now pick a mouth, open it, and say...

59
00:03:42.588 --> 00:03:43.589
Uh...

60
00:03:45.007 --> 00:03:47.385
What? My mother was a saint!

61
00:03:47.468 --> 00:03:48.594
Get out!

62
00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:58.521
Dear Lord, Bender, you're filthy.

63
00:03:58.854 --> 00:04:01.482
Yeah, like you don't
have crap in your neck.

64
00:04:01.732 --> 00:04:03.651
Amy, why don't you give his body

65
00:04:03.734 --> 00:04:05.444
a going-over with the cleaning pick?

66
00:04:05.528 --> 00:04:06.654
Okay.

67
00:04:06.737 --> 00:04:08.697
Does it hurt when I go like this?

68
00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:09.824
Ow!

69
00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:10.991
A little.

70
00:04:11.242 --> 00:04:13.703
Well, the doctor says
I'm as healthy as a crab.

71
00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.037
Can I go into space now?

72
00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:17.248
As soon as we finish cleaning Bender.

73
00:04:17.331 --> 00:04:18.416
Oh, and Fry...

74
00:04:18.499 --> 00:04:20.960
This is our intern, Amy Wong.

75
00:04:21.043 --> 00:04:22.962
She's an engineering student of mine.

76
00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:24.505
I like having her around

77
00:04:24.588 --> 00:04:26.632
because she has
the same blood type as me.

78
00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:31.262
Hey, you're the unfrozen guy
from the 20th century, right?

79
00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:33.013
Last time I checked.

80
00:04:33.264 --> 00:04:36.308
Hang on. Amy Wong, of the Mars Wongs?

81
00:04:36.392 --> 00:04:38.519
Look, we're not as rich as everybody says.

82
00:04:38.602 --> 00:04:41.439
Uh-huh. What sorority do you belong to?

83
00:04:41.772 --> 00:04:42.898
Kappa Kappa Wong.

84
00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:44.066
Hey, rich girl!

85
00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:46.193
Look over here.
It's me, Bender.

86
00:04:46.277 --> 00:04:47.945
I'm being entertaining.

87
00:04:48.028 --> 00:04:50.072
La-la-la, look at my head

88
00:04:50.156 --> 00:04:52.366
It's okay to look at my head

89
00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:55.077
I got a big ol' head
And hey! Ho!

90
00:04:55.494 --> 00:04:57.288
All right, show's over. I'm tired.

91
00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:59.540
Ah, to be young again...

92
00:04:59.623 --> 00:05:01.125
And also a robot.

93
00:05:01.375 --> 00:05:02.585
Oh! Now, as I recall,

94
00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:04.754
you youngsters
have a package to deliver.

95
00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:07.965
Finally. Come on, Bender.
Let's mosey.

96
00:05:10.968 --> 00:05:12.344
Nice catch, idiot.

97
00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:19.477
So, where are we going anyway?

98
00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:21.187
Nowhere special, the moon.

99
00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:22.396
The moo... The moon?

100
00:05:22.605 --> 00:05:23.606
The moon moon?

101
00:05:23.689 --> 00:05:27.026
Wow, I'm going to be a famous hero
just like Neil Armstrong

102
00:05:27.109 --> 00:05:29.487
and those other brave guys
no one ever heard of.

103
00:05:29.695 --> 00:05:31.864
Oh! I love stuff like the moon.

104
00:05:31.947 --> 00:05:33.032
Can I come, Leela?

105
00:05:33.115 --> 00:05:35.659
Well... I guess so.

106
00:05:35.743 --> 00:05:36.869
Just be careful.

107
00:05:36.952 --> 00:05:38.788
I'd like to hold off
any major screw-ups

108
00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:40.956
until at least
my second day as captain.

109
00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.958
Nothing will go wrong.

110
00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:45.252
If something goes wrong
bring back the blood.

111
00:05:53.469 --> 00:05:54.470
Can I do the countdown?

112
00:05:54.553 --> 00:05:55.763
Huh? Oh, sure.

113
00:05:55.846 --> 00:05:56.931
Knock yourself out.

114
00:05:57.014 --> 00:05:58.808
Ten, nine...

115
00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:00.184
Okay, we're here.

116
00:06:00.351 --> 00:06:02.436
...eight, seven, six, five,
four, three, two, one. Blastoff.

117
00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:13.489
Hurry up.
I want to see the moon.

118
00:06:13.572 --> 00:06:15.783
Relax, it's open till 9:00.

119
00:06:16.242 --> 00:06:18.994
That's one small step for Fry...

120
00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:21.872
And one giant line for admission.

121
00:06:22.832 --> 00:06:24.959
Wow!

122
00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:26.752
Um... Can I have cuts?

123
00:06:26.836 --> 00:06:29.130
Hmm... Mmm...

124
00:06:29.338 --> 00:06:30.506
No!

125
00:06:35.094 --> 00:06:36.595
You're not going to believe this,

126
00:06:36.679 --> 00:06:38.973
but they landed
an amusement park on the moon.

127
00:06:39.098 --> 00:06:41.934
Guh! It's the happiest place
orbiting earth.

128
00:06:42.017 --> 00:06:43.352
Let's go already.

129
00:06:43.436 --> 00:06:45.396
Fry, we have a crate to deliver.

130
00:06:45.521 --> 00:06:48.274
Let's just dump it in the sewer
and say we delivered it.

131
00:06:48.357 --> 00:06:49.400
Too much work.

132
00:06:49.483 --> 00:06:51.777
Let's burn it and say
we dumped it in the sewer.

133
00:06:51.944 --> 00:06:54.822
Okay, if everyone's finished
being stupid...

134
00:06:54.905 --> 00:06:56.699
I had more, but you go ahead.

135
00:06:56.782 --> 00:06:58.743
We'll deliver that crate
like professionals

136
00:06:58.826 --> 00:07:00.077
and then we'll go home.

137
00:07:00.286 --> 00:07:02.329
But I've never been
to the moon before.

138
00:07:02.872 --> 00:07:04.582
Oh, all right.

139
00:07:04.665 --> 00:07:06.834
We'll deliver that crate
like professionals

140
00:07:06.917 --> 00:07:09.045
And then we'll go
ride the bumper cars.

141
00:07:11.338 --> 00:07:13.924
Amy, why don't you help Fry
hoist down the crate?

142
00:07:14.175 --> 00:07:15.509
Then lock up when you're done.

143
00:07:15.593 --> 00:07:16.969
Just be careful.

144
00:07:17.053 --> 00:07:19.680
Aye, aye, Captain.
I mean, only one eye.

145
00:07:19.972 --> 00:07:21.932
I mean, yes, sir... um, ma'am.

146
00:07:22.767 --> 00:07:24.351
- Clear?
- Clear.

147
00:07:24.435 --> 00:07:26.228
- Ready to hoist?
- Ready.

148
00:07:27.772 --> 00:07:28.898
Ow!

149
00:07:36.572 --> 00:07:38.491
My first space delivery.

150
00:07:38.783 --> 00:07:40.451
Greetings, moon man.

151
00:07:40.534 --> 00:07:41.702
We come in peace.

152
00:07:42.036 --> 00:07:44.205
I am Fry, from the planet Earth.

153
00:07:44.497 --> 00:07:45.664
Wise guy, huh?

154
00:07:45.915 --> 00:07:48.501
If I wasn't so lazy
I'd punch you in the stomach.

155
00:07:48.709 --> 00:07:50.086
But you are lazy, right?

156
00:07:50.252 --> 00:07:52.088
Oh, don't get me started.

157
00:08:05.643 --> 00:08:07.978
Hi! I'm Craterface.

158
00:08:08.062 --> 00:08:09.897
Welcome to Luna Park.

159
00:08:09.980 --> 00:08:12.566
I'll have to confiscate
your alcohol, sir.

160
00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:15.361
Better mascots than you have tried.

161
00:08:18.864 --> 00:08:21.575
At least I still have my self-respect.

162
00:08:32.628 --> 00:08:35.172
Ugh, who buys this trash?

163
00:08:35.381 --> 00:08:38.259
Idiots who need gifts for other idiots.

164
00:08:38.342 --> 00:08:40.720
Hey, I got you guys
refrigerator magnets.

165
00:08:43.389 --> 00:08:44.640
Get it off. Get it off!

166
00:08:44.724 --> 00:08:45.766
Get it... Uh-oh.

167
00:08:46.308 --> 00:08:50.521
How many roads
must a man walk down

168
00:08:50.604 --> 00:08:52.314
Before you...

169
00:08:57.611 --> 00:08:59.447
Keep those things off of me.

170
00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:01.991
Magnets screw up my inhibition unit.

171
00:09:02.199 --> 00:09:05.494
So you flip out and start acting
like some crazy folk singer?

172
00:09:05.619 --> 00:09:08.831
Yes. I guess a robot
would have to be crazy

173
00:09:08.914 --> 00:09:11.125
to want to be a folk singer.

174
00:09:13.753 --> 00:09:17.798
We're whalers on the moon,
we carry a harpoon

175
00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:20.259
But there ain't no whales,
so we tell tall tales

176
00:09:20.342 --> 00:09:22.511
And sing our whaling tune

177
00:09:22.595 --> 00:09:25.014
Bender! Hey, Bender! Over here!

178
00:09:25.097 --> 00:09:28.476
Oh, geez, I went to
high school with that guy.

179
00:09:28.684 --> 00:09:30.352
Monsanto presents...

180
00:09:30.436 --> 00:09:32.521
The Goophy Gopher Revue.

181
00:09:33.314 --> 00:09:37.109
Why does a moon rock
taste better than an earth rock?

182
00:09:37.234 --> 00:09:40.029
Because it's a little "meteor."

183
00:09:44.492 --> 00:09:45.701
This is weak.

184
00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:49.205
Address all complaints
to the Monsanto corporation.

185
00:09:52.083 --> 00:09:53.209
What's wrong, Fry?

186
00:09:53.292 --> 00:09:54.543
I don't know.

187
00:09:54.627 --> 00:09:57.463
This place is great and all
but it's just so artificial.

188
00:09:57.671 --> 00:10:00.132
The gravity, the air, the gophers.

189
00:10:00.216 --> 00:10:01.592
You might as well stay on earth.

190
00:10:02.551 --> 00:10:04.095
That's what I came to see.

191
00:10:05.471 --> 00:10:07.640
I want to go out there
and jump around like an astronaut.

192
00:10:07.765 --> 00:10:09.308
Screw this phony stuff.

193
00:10:09.392 --> 00:10:11.435
But the phony stuff is what's fun.

194
00:10:11.519 --> 00:10:12.686
It's boring out there.

195
00:10:12.812 --> 00:10:15.648
Yeah. You're the kind of guy
who visits Jerusalem

196
00:10:15.731 --> 00:10:18.025
and doesn't want to see
the "Sexateria."

197
00:10:18.442 --> 00:10:21.946
Maybe I should take Fry
on the Lunar Rover Ride.

198
00:10:22.029 --> 00:10:24.907
You get to wear a space suit
and drive around on the surface

199
00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:27.118
And the line's short
because it's educational.

200
00:10:27.326 --> 00:10:29.203
I don't care how educational it is.

201
00:10:29.286 --> 00:10:30.413
Let's do it!

202
00:10:30.955 --> 00:10:33.749
Next year in Jerusalem!

203
00:10:34.834 --> 00:10:35.960
Two adults, please.

204
00:10:36.043 --> 00:10:39.255
Finally, get ready
for some serious moon action.

205
00:10:42.258 --> 00:10:44.510
The story of lunar exploration

206
00:10:44.593 --> 00:10:47.888
started with one man...
A man with a dream.

207
00:10:48.556 --> 00:10:50.725
One of these days, Alice.

208
00:10:50.808 --> 00:10:54.937
Bang! Zoom!
Straight to the moon!

209
00:10:55.396 --> 00:10:59.191
Wow. I never realized
the first astronauts were so fat.

210
00:10:59.650 --> 00:11:02.361
That's not an astronaut.
It's a TV comedian.

211
00:11:02.445 --> 00:11:06.031
He was just using space travel
as a metaphor for beating his wife.

212
00:11:11.746 --> 00:11:15.458
Wow! I could swear I was
really playing Virtual Skeeball.

213
00:11:15.541 --> 00:11:17.251
- Hmm?
- Look, it's that crate

214
00:11:17.334 --> 00:11:19.045
we were going to throw in the sewer.

215
00:11:23.007 --> 00:11:24.341
The keys to the ship!

216
00:11:24.717 --> 00:11:26.343
They must have fallen into the crate.

217
00:11:26.469 --> 00:11:28.888
Leela's going to kill me.

218
00:11:28.971 --> 00:11:31.682
Nah. She'll probably make me do it.

219
00:11:32.016 --> 00:11:34.518
Mister, could you please
get those keys out for me?

220
00:11:34.602 --> 00:11:37.229
What do I look like,
a guy who's not lazy?

221
00:11:49.158 --> 00:11:53.704
No one knows where,
when or how man first landed on the moon.

222
00:11:53.829 --> 00:11:56.791
- I do.
- But our fungineers think

223
00:11:56.874 --> 00:11:59.627
It might have happened
something like this.

224
00:12:00.252 --> 00:12:02.505
We're whalers on the moon

225
00:12:02.588 --> 00:12:04.590
We carry a harpoon

226
00:12:04.965 --> 00:12:07.218
But there ain't no whales
so we tell tall tales

227
00:12:07.426 --> 00:12:09.261
And sing a whaling tune

228
00:12:09.387 --> 00:12:11.555
That's not how it happened.

229
00:12:11.639 --> 00:12:14.350
Oh, really? I don't see you
with a fungineering degree.

230
00:12:14.475 --> 00:12:15.976
This is stupid.

231
00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:18.062
I'm taking this thing
out to the real moon.

232
00:12:18.145 --> 00:12:20.314
Fry, no. This is my first mission

233
00:12:20.398 --> 00:12:22.733
and I'm not going to let us
get in any trouble.

234
00:12:22.817 --> 00:12:24.443
Besides, the car's on a track.

235
00:12:24.527 --> 00:12:25.528
Not for long.

236
00:12:28.531 --> 00:12:29.573
We're whalers...

237
00:12:29.657 --> 00:12:31.075
Oh! Ow!

238
00:12:31.158 --> 00:12:33.494
I died doing what I loved.

239
00:12:34.286 --> 00:12:36.455
Okay, you're on the surface.

240
00:12:36.539 --> 00:12:37.873
Now, I'll give you ten minutes.

241
00:12:37.957 --> 00:12:39.834
then you'll get bored, turn around

242
00:12:39.917 --> 00:12:42.044
and apologize for being such a jerk.

243
00:12:42.128 --> 00:12:43.713
- Agreed?
- Agreed.

244
00:12:43.921 --> 00:12:45.339
Yee-ha!

245
00:12:47.174 --> 00:12:48.926
Yeah! Crank up the radio!

246
00:12:49.427 --> 00:12:51.303
We're whalers on the...

247
00:12:52.096 --> 00:12:53.681
Yee-ha!

248
00:12:57.059 --> 00:12:59.562
Time's up.
Make a U-turn at the next crater.

249
00:12:59.645 --> 00:13:00.646
No, not yet.

250
00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:02.982
How about we go look
for the original moon landing site?

251
00:13:03.065 --> 00:13:05.359
That's crazy.
It's been lost for centuries.

252
00:13:05.443 --> 00:13:07.403
Well, I'm feeling lucky.

253
00:13:07.486 --> 00:13:08.612
Ooh.

254
00:13:13.701 --> 00:13:16.412
Uh... I'm ready to go back now.

255
00:13:19.623 --> 00:13:22.251
We're going to die!
It's every man for himself!

256
00:13:22.626 --> 00:13:23.627
Help me, Leela!

257
00:13:28.591 --> 00:13:30.426
Whoo!

258
00:13:34.847 --> 00:13:35.848
You did it.

259
00:13:35.931 --> 00:13:36.932
We're safe.

260
00:13:37.266 --> 00:13:39.185
No. Now we're going to die.

261
00:13:40.436 --> 00:13:42.229
It's every man for himself!

262
00:13:46.942 --> 00:13:49.278
Hey, look what I won
from a tourist's pocket.

263
00:13:49.361 --> 00:13:51.405
Shut up. You're distracting me.

264
00:13:51.655 --> 00:13:53.699
Come on, it's just like making love.

265
00:13:53.783 --> 00:13:57.495
You know, left, down,
rotate 62 degrees

266
00:13:57.578 --> 00:13:58.871
Engage rotor.

267
00:13:58.954 --> 00:14:00.915
I know how to make love.

268
00:14:03.376 --> 00:14:04.710
Here, let me do it.

269
00:14:09.757 --> 00:14:11.967
Oh, lousy arm must be rigged.

270
00:14:13.886 --> 00:14:15.179
That's her, officers.

271
00:14:15.262 --> 00:14:17.723
That's the woman
who programmed me for evil.

272
00:14:23.687 --> 00:14:28.150
Yeah, well, I'm going to go
build my own theme park

273
00:14:28.234 --> 00:14:30.236
With blackjack and hookers.

274
00:14:30.319 --> 00:14:32.571
In fact, forget the park.

275
00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:39.161
I'm sorry, Leela.

276
00:14:39.245 --> 00:14:40.871
I can't go on any further.

277
00:14:40.955 --> 00:14:43.499
Just leave me to die
in that barn over there.

278
00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:51.924
Oh, thank God.

279
00:14:54.051 --> 00:14:55.428
Trespassers, eh?

280
00:14:55.636 --> 00:14:57.930
No, sir. We're amusement park patrons.

281
00:14:58.097 --> 00:15:00.808
Ooh, that's a wicked, sinful place.

282
00:15:01.058 --> 00:15:04.019
Tilt-a-whirl's okay,
but the rest is mighty wicked.

283
00:15:04.270 --> 00:15:06.230
Our car broke down
and we're out of oxygen.

284
00:15:06.313 --> 00:15:07.481
Can we borrow some?

285
00:15:07.565 --> 00:15:12.236
"Borry?" Looky here, city girl,
oxygen don't grow on trees.

286
00:15:12.403 --> 00:15:15.573
You'll have to earn it doing chores
on my hydroponic farm.

287
00:15:15.656 --> 00:15:18.701
You can go back to your precious
theme park at sunup.

288
00:15:18.993 --> 00:15:21.287
I guess we could do chores
for a few hours.

289
00:15:21.370 --> 00:15:23.831
Fry, night lasts two weeks on the moon.

290
00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:27.168
Yep. Drops down to minus 173.

291
00:15:27.334 --> 00:15:29.086
Fahrenheit or Celsius?

292
00:15:29.253 --> 00:15:31.047
First one, then the other.

293
00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:35.176
And them space suits ain't a-heated
so you ain't going nowhere till sunrise.

294
00:15:35.259 --> 00:15:36.594
You can sleep in the barn.

295
00:15:36.761 --> 00:15:38.971
Just don't be a-touchin'

296
00:15:39.055 --> 00:15:42.141
my three beautiful
robot daughters, you hear?

297
00:15:42.433 --> 00:15:43.809
Robot daughters?

298
00:15:44.101 --> 00:15:45.811
This here's Lulabelle 7...

299
00:15:45.895 --> 00:15:47.229
Yoo-hoo.

300
00:15:47.313 --> 00:15:49.356
Daisy Mae 128-K...

301
00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:51.067
Yoo-hoo.

302
00:15:51.150 --> 00:15:52.860
And the Crushinator.

303
00:15:54.570 --> 00:15:56.238
Yoo-hoo.

304
00:15:56.530 --> 00:15:57.823
Whoa!

305
00:15:58.324 --> 00:16:01.118
I told you to turn around
and go back to the park.

306
00:16:01.369 --> 00:16:03.746
But, oh, no.
The park was too phony.

307
00:16:03.829 --> 00:16:05.373
We had to see the real moon.

308
00:16:05.539 --> 00:16:06.707
And it was great.

309
00:16:06.791 --> 00:16:08.376
We got to see craters and rocks

310
00:16:08.459 --> 00:16:11.045
and that one incredible rock
that looked like a crater

311
00:16:11.128 --> 00:16:12.213
And... And these fellas.

312
00:16:14.382 --> 00:16:16.801
Fry, face it, the moon is a dump.

313
00:16:16.884 --> 00:16:18.928
It's a boring dried-up wasteland.

314
00:16:19.011 --> 00:16:21.013
And the only reason
anybody ever comes here

315
00:16:21.097 --> 00:16:23.265
is for the tacky
little amusement park.

316
00:16:23.349 --> 00:16:24.683
Can't you just accept that?

317
00:16:24.767 --> 00:16:27.103
I guess I can't.

318
00:16:28.813 --> 00:16:31.816
I'll learn you to sleep
with my robot daughters.

319
00:16:33.567 --> 00:16:36.153
He'll never find me in here.

320
00:16:36.362 --> 00:16:37.363
Bender?

321
00:16:37.488 --> 00:16:40.866
Ugh. Bender, you didn't touch
the Crushinator, did you?

322
00:16:41.409 --> 00:16:44.662
Of course not. A lady that fine
you got to romance first.

323
00:16:57.299 --> 00:16:58.634
Oh, no, you don't.

324
00:16:58.718 --> 00:17:00.052
Come here, Crushinator.

325
00:17:00.136 --> 00:17:01.929
Yes, Pa.

326
00:17:19.321 --> 00:17:20.906
- It's too low!
- Hang on.

327
00:17:21.031 --> 00:17:22.408
Hang on. Jump!

328
00:17:27.913 --> 00:17:29.248
Hold on to your helmet.

329
00:17:29.457 --> 00:17:31.083
Whoa!

330
00:17:36.756 --> 00:17:38.007
- Yes!
- Oh, boy.

331
00:17:42.928 --> 00:17:45.973
Goldurn it, Crushinator, jump!

332
00:17:46.057 --> 00:17:49.560
No, Pa. I love him.

333
00:17:50.352 --> 00:17:52.605
Oh!

334
00:17:54.065 --> 00:17:57.026
Hey, cool. Dark side of the moon.

335
00:17:57.193 --> 00:17:58.778
Nightfall's coming.

336
00:18:00.988 --> 00:18:02.573
Hurry, before we freeze.

337
00:18:02.823 --> 00:18:04.742
What do you mean we, mammal?

338
00:18:12.458 --> 00:18:13.459
Oh, dear.

339
00:18:13.542 --> 00:18:15.795
I really ought to do something.

340
00:18:15.878 --> 00:18:18.923
But I'm already in my pajamas.

341
00:18:24.345 --> 00:18:25.971
We can't outrun it forever.

342
00:18:26.764 --> 00:18:28.808
Over there. Look!

343
00:18:29.433 --> 00:18:30.851
It's the moon landing site.

344
00:18:31.060 --> 00:18:32.144
We found it.

345
00:18:37.900 --> 00:18:39.068
Quick, get in.

346
00:18:40.277 --> 00:18:43.155
It's that flag from MTV.

347
00:18:43.239 --> 00:18:45.491
And Neil Armstrong's footprint.

348
00:18:46.826 --> 00:18:48.494
Hey, my foot's bigger.

349
00:18:48.869 --> 00:18:51.789
Leela, isn't this the greatest
thing you've ever seen?

350
00:18:52.123 --> 00:18:53.582
Fry, look around.

351
00:18:53.708 --> 00:18:57.378
It's just a crummy plastic flag
and a dead man's tracks in the dust.

352
00:19:01.590 --> 00:19:03.759
Now, get in here before you freeze.

353
00:19:13.519 --> 00:19:15.855
Oh, no room for Bender, huh?

354
00:19:15.938 --> 00:19:18.899
Fine, I'll go build my own lunar lander

355
00:19:18.983 --> 00:19:21.694
With blackjack and hookers.

356
00:19:21.777 --> 00:19:25.030
In fact, forget the lunar lander
and the blackjack.

357
00:19:25.114 --> 00:19:26.824
Ah, screw the whole thing.

358
00:19:27.324 --> 00:19:29.243
Well, if the oxygen holds out,

359
00:19:29.326 --> 00:19:31.328
we might live long enough
to starve to death.

360
00:19:31.579 --> 00:19:35.249
Look, Leela, I'm sorry.
I never should have dragged you out here.

361
00:19:35.458 --> 00:19:37.460
That's right. You shouldn't have.

362
00:19:37.543 --> 00:19:39.670
I still don't get
what the big attraction is.

363
00:19:40.337 --> 00:19:42.715
I never told anybody this

364
00:19:42.798 --> 00:19:45.509
but a thousand years ago,
I used to look up at the moon

365
00:19:45.593 --> 00:19:47.261
and dream about being an astronaut.

366
00:19:47.344 --> 00:19:50.556
I just didn't have the grades
or the physical endurance.

367
00:19:50.639 --> 00:19:51.807
Plus, I threw up a lot

368
00:19:51.891 --> 00:19:53.768
and nobody likes
spending a week with me.

369
00:19:53.851 --> 00:19:55.603
A week would be a little much.

370
00:19:55.811 --> 00:19:59.523
The moon was like this awesome,
romantic, mysterious thing

371
00:19:59.607 --> 00:20:02.193
hanging up there in the sky
where you could never reach it

372
00:20:02.276 --> 00:20:04.070
no matter how much you wanted to.

373
00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:06.822
But you're right.

374
00:20:06.906 --> 00:20:09.909
Once you're actually here,
it's just a big dull rock.

375
00:20:09.992 --> 00:20:12.745
I guess I just wanted you
to see it through my eyes

376
00:20:12.953 --> 00:20:14.163
The way I used to.

377
00:20:18.834 --> 00:20:20.252
Fry, look.

378
00:20:21.921 --> 00:20:24.048
It really is beautiful.

379
00:20:24.465 --> 00:20:26.759
I don't know why
I never noticed before.

380
00:20:36.143 --> 00:20:39.438
Had to come back
for the Crushinator, eh, robot?

381
00:20:39.522 --> 00:20:41.357
Well, I got you this time.

382
00:20:50.658 --> 00:20:52.743
It's Amy. We're saved.

383
00:20:52.993 --> 00:20:54.203
Amy?

384
00:20:54.286 --> 00:20:56.747
Where'd she learn to operate
the controls like that?

385
00:21:05.214 --> 00:21:06.424
Not the magnet.

386
00:21:06.507 --> 00:21:09.760
No! No! No!

387
00:21:09.844 --> 00:21:10.928
Uh-oh.

388
00:21:13.597 --> 00:21:16.934
She'll be coming around
the mountain when she comes

389
00:21:17.017 --> 00:21:19.687
She'll be coming around
the mountain when she comes

390
00:21:19.770 --> 00:21:20.980
I'll kill you, Amy!

391
00:21:21.063 --> 00:21:22.565
She'll be coming around the mountain

392
00:21:22.648 --> 00:21:24.233
She'll be coming around
the mountain, she'll be...

393
00:21:29.321 --> 00:21:30.531
Ah, dang it.

394
00:21:37.621 --> 00:21:42.126
She'll be riding six
white horses when she comes

395
00:21:42.209 --> 00:21:44.420
She'll be riding six
whitehorses when she comes

396
00:21:44.503 --> 00:21:45.546
Hey, I'm pretty good.

397
00:21:45.629 --> 00:21:47.381
She'll be riding
six white horses

398
00:21:47.465 --> 00:21:49.508
So, Fry, was the real moon

399
00:21:49.592 --> 00:21:52.136
anything like the moon
you used to dream about?

400
00:21:52.219 --> 00:21:54.263
Uh... Close enough.

401
00:21:55.598 --> 00:21:59.143
Well, I'll shoot her
with my ray-gun when she comes

402
00:21:59.477 --> 00:22:02.646
Yes, I'll shoot her
with my ray-gun when she comes

403
00:22:02.730 --> 00:22:06.025
Yes, I'll shoot her with my ray-gun
Oh, I'llshoot her with my ray-gun

404
00:22:06.108 --> 00:22:09.111
Yes, I'll shoot her withmy ray-gun
when she comes, when she comes

405
00:22:09.195 --> 00:22:12.114
I'll be blasting
all the humans in the world

406
00:22:12.198 --> 00:22:15.284
I'll be blasting
all the humans in the world

407
00:22:15.368 --> 00:22:18.788
I'll be blasting all the humans
I'll be blasting all the humans

408
00:22:18.871 --> 00:22:20.998
I'll be blasting
all the humans in the world

409
00:22:21.082 --> 00:22:22.291
In the world

410
00:22:22.416 --> 00:22:25.378
One more time!

